meson (Windows): a static library is built without a resource compiler

For Windows, FreeType's meson.build compiles a version resource
(src/base/ftver.rc) into the library, whatever kind of library it is,
and meson stops when it finds no resource compiler.

A version resource is what Explorer shows of a DLL. A static library
has none: its objects go into somebody else's DLL, which has a version
of its own. Ceau's FreeType for Windows is such a library (it is linked
into ass.dll), and it is compiled on a Mac with the swift.org toolchain,
which brings no resource compiler. The resource is now compiled only
when a DLL is built.

--- a/meson.build	2026-11-19 00:55:42
+++ b/meson.build	2026-11-19 00:55:42
@@ -238,11 +238,13 @@
 
 ft2_sources += 'src/dlg/dlgwrap.c'
 if host_machine.system() == 'windows'
-  winmod = import('windows')
-  ft2_sources += [
-    'builds/windows/ftdebug.c',
-    winmod.compile_resources('src/base/ftver.rc'),
-  ]
+  ft2_sources += 'builds/windows/ftdebug.c'
+  # The version resource is a DLL's. A static library carries none, and so
+  # needs no resource compiler to be built.
+  if get_option('default_library') != 'static'
+    winmod = import('windows')
+    ft2_sources += winmod.compile_resources('src/base/ftver.rc')
+  endif
 else
   ft2_sources += 'src/base/ftdebug.c'
 endif
